</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study the Portmanteau theorem for weak convergence of probability
measures.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate Prokhorov's theorem and the role of tightness.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study uniform integrability and prove a version of Vitali's convergence
theorem.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate martingales as sequences defined by conditional
expectations.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Study filtrations, stopping times, and optional sampling.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Investigate <m>L^p</m> spaces as Banach spaces and <m>L^2</m> as a Hilbert
